sentences.t:
Nisus erat portae custos, acerrimus armis,
Hyrtacides, comitem Aeneae quem miserat Ida
venatrix iaculo celerem levibusque sagittis;

sentences.l:
Nisus was of the gate the guard, keenest in arms,
son of Hyrtacus, as comrade to Aeneas whom had sent Ida,
the huntress, with javelin quick and with light arrows;

sentences.t:
Sed siquis, quae multa vides discrimine tali,
siquis in adversum rapiat casusve deusve,
te superesse velim;

sentences.l:
But if anyone, as many you see in a crisis such,
if anyone to ruin should sweep, either chance or a god,
you to survive I would wish;
